WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.110
Let's make Winter twig stars.

2
00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:07.229
Arrange five similar twigs in a star, then secure the five outer points with

3
00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:08.245
short string ties.

4
00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:10.410
Make and display it indoors.

5
00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.870
Make this project with a grown-up.

6
00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.980
Gather the supplies listed below the video.

7
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.605
Pause whenever you need more time.

8
00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:23.340
An adult prepares twigs, ties or checks the joins and trims loose string.

9
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.850
Display flat; do not wear it or leave string decorations outdoors.

10
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:30.523
Step 1.

11
00:00:30.903 --> 00:00:32.833
Make a five-point guide.

12
00:00:33.213 --> 00:00:37.560
Draw five dots around a circle on paper: one at the top, two at

13
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.423
the sides and two lower down.

14
00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:42.573
Number them around the circle 1 to 5.

15
00:00:42.953 --> 00:00:45.763
Join 1 to 3 to 5 to 2 to 4 to 1.

16
00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:47.523
Grown-up help.

17
00:00:47.903 --> 00:00:50.283
Prepare smooth twigs of similar length.

18
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.847
Step 2.

19
00:00:53.227 --> 00:00:54.767
Lay the five twigs.

20
00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:57.732
Lay a twig along each line of the guide.

21
00:00:58.112 --> 00:01:02.027
Let twig ends overlap by about 2 centimetres at each outer point.

22
00:01:02.407 --> 00:01:05.807
Keep the star flat and adjust until the points are even.

23
00:01:06.187 --> 00:01:07.567
Grown-up help.

24
00:01:07.947 --> 00:01:10.647
Help keep the overlapping twigs in place.

25
00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.512
Step 3.

26
00:01:13.892 --> 00:01:15.667
Tie the first two points.

27
00:01:16.047 --> 00:01:20.383
At one outer point, wrap a short string around the two overlapping twig ends

28
00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:22.552
three times, then tie a double knot.

29
00:01:22.932 --> 00:01:26.632
Repeat at the next point while an adult holds the star flat.

30
00:01:27.012 --> 00:01:28.392
Grown-up help.

31
00:01:28.772 --> 00:01:31.277
Tie or check the knots and hold the layout.

32
00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:33.817
Step 4.

33
00:01:34.197 --> 00:01:36.027
Secure the remaining points.

34
00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:39.412
Tie the remaining three outer points the same way.

35
00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:42.822
Gently lift one edge to check the shape holds.

36
00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:47.122
Tighten a loose join, then have an adult trim long string tails.

37
00:01:47.502 --> 00:01:48.882
Grown-up help.

38
00:01:49.262 --> 00:01:51.717
Finish knots and trim string tails.

39
00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:54.342
Step 5.

40
00:01:54.722 --> 00:01:56.487
Display your winter star.

41
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:00.047
Remove the paper guide and lay the star on a shelf.

42
00:02:00.427 --> 00:02:04.017
Tuck a small paper snowflake under a tie if desired.

43
00:02:04.397 --> 00:02:07.917
Keep it away from heat, flames and younger children.

44
00:02:08.297 --> 00:02:09.677
Grown-up help.

45
00:02:10.057 --> 00:02:12.712
Check the star and display location.

46
00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:17.082
Here are three ideas for your finished project.

47
00:02:17.462 --> 00:02:21.012
These example pictures were made with artificial intelligence.

48
00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:23.412
Your creation can look different.

49
00:02:23.792 --> 00:02:27.537
Untie string for reuse and sort untreated twigs separately.

50
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:31.072
Keep dry indoors and inspect knots before moving.

51
00:02:31.452 --> 00:02:32.442
Well done.

52
00:02:32.822 --> 00:02:35.252
Take a moment to enjoy what you made.

